[h1]Phobos Framework[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.130.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Public since 7 October 2026

The shared controls, crew work and supplies behind the Phobos mods.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Crew standing orders: give crew a chosen job and approved supplies. Orders begin disabled; shifts, needs, access and the game's AutoTask and Haul duties still apply. Crew take supplies from anywhere aboard, nearest first, never from weapons, chargers or toilets.
[*]Crew study Phobos specialities at powered terminals through the game's own study actions.
[*]Upkeep for long hauls, off until chosen: idle crew tune machines (up to 10% faster, for more power), inspect them, put deck clutter away and practise skills.
[*]Onboard work carries on through time-skip (StepSeconds sets the pace); exterior work and flight wait for Resume.
[*]Construction, transfers and purchases check materials, space and power; a full destination keeps cargo where it was.
[*]Press twice to go ahead: a change that needs machines paused or an old link removed says what it will do; press again to do it.
[*]Shared gas and process-water lines (INSTALL, HVAC) and a conveyor belt (MISC). A line joins each machine or store it runs under or beside; touching equipment chains like pipe; nothing links over open floor. Lines hold what flows through them: drain one into a D20 canister (vent a gas line) before taking it up, then pour the canister into a tank.
[*]Rivetline S2 to S5 process water silos for every mod, shared bulk storage in three sizes that shows its contents on right-click, canisters and suit bottles filled to 99%, honest mass, and station sales and 45% buy-back under the refuelling kiosk's Bulk supplies.
[*]RCS thrusters push by each gas's real cold-gas worth; readings count in nitrogen-equivalent kilograms. Content mods can add propellant feeds.
[*]A Phobos autopilot turns off only the sensors it switched on. Your own switch always wins, and the crew log says so every time.
[*]Content mods can put back the game's own build sites for destroyed parts, add PDA apps with live charts and tie content to stations as stories do.
[*]Shared merchant stock, kiosk offers, salvage, repair, Restore and dismantling rules.
[*]Machines give off a quarter of their heat (MachineHeatScale) and hum while they work, as loud as the game's own scrubber; the sounds are WAV files you can swap.
[*]Data packs: each content mod's tables (prices, work, salvage, recipes, odds) ship as read-only copies; your own files in BepInEx/config override them, checked first; recipes conserve mass. Share them as an add-on.
[*]Story content from data files anyone can write: TV news and adverts, goal chains with rewards, small talk, loading tips, encyclopedia articles and data files, tied to stations, threads, named people (goals show their faces), standing and the clock. Click a story goal to read its letters and reply. Removing a story file never breaks a save.
[/list]

[h2]Fair gig deadlines[/h2]
The game gives a far gig 70 hours per AU in a straight line, quicker than its own ferry. Framework times the trip for each torch ship you own (accelerate at the game's 2 g limiter, brake to arrive), averages them, adds a quarter and 4 hours to dock and turn in, and never shortens the game's own time. 0.7 AU at 1 g: 49 hours becomes 76. Speed bonuses follow. No torch ship: the game's time stands. Settings: Gigs.

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*]Install Framework with the Phobos content mods you want; each names the Framework version it needs.
[*]Right-click Phobos equipment: Control Panel for its settings, Maintenance for its crew order, upkeep and removal checks. Each crew page has an About button that opens the encyclopedia's Phobos operations articles.
[*]In the F3 console, phobosframework status reports what loaded, phobosframework crew who could take each order step and why, phobosframework loot a mining table as the game rolls it; save-changing tests need unlockdebug.
[/list]
Mod authors: see the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/development/framework-author-guide.md]Framework author guide[/url].

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[*]Optional: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3757331189]Valtora's Ship's Water[/url] (its tanks join and fill water lines), [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3789049955]LOGUSS's Common Sense modules[/url] and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3788237703]jossla's Study at Terminals[/url] work alongside it. They remain their authors' work; linking implies no endorsement.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Framework and the Phobos content mods you want.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it so they load; repeat after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[*]Remove any copies from the repository's local installer first, so only one loads. See the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/installing-mods.md]installation guide[/url].
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
Ordinary saves are supported. Keep Framework and the content mods installed while a save uses their content; removal is not a clean uninstall. Saved contents or settings that cannot be checked safely stop the affected work for inspection. A data file that breaks a rule is skipped, with the reason in the log. Automated checks pass; in-game evaluation of recent features is ongoing.

[h2]Credits and sources[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games, Kitfox Games or any research institution cited in the guides. Research informs the design; compact equipment, yields and operating limits remain gameplay choices.
Artwork and machine sounds (ElevenLabs, elevenlabs.io) are AI-assisted; provenance and terms are recorded separately.

